🛑 Problem
Health insurance companies need to pay medical bills for their clients while keeping their finances stable.
If they miscalculate, they might:

Lose money (too many claims vs. premiums).

Set premiums too high (lose clients).

The difficulty:

Medical costs can change suddenly.

New rules (like covering new treatments) can increase costs.

Without good forecasting, they risk financial instability.

🎯 Goal of the Project
Build a system that:

Predicts future medical expenses.

Simulates how changes in coverage rules will affect costs.

Helps decision-makers choose the best policies to stay profitable.

📋 Your Job
Collect & prepare data (medical history, client profiles, benefit rules).

Train multiple models (regression, decision trees, XGBoost, LSTM, etc.).

Compare models and pick the most accurate.

Create a simulation tool (dashboard/API) where the user can:

Enter changes in coverage.

Instantly see the predicted financial impact.

Deliver a report & present results to the technical team.


